KNOWNBUG with the headers of libstdc++ 16 (gcc 16) only; passes with gcc 11-15
headers.  Reproduce by preprocessing with g++-16 -E (the predefined macros
select the code paths) and running cbmc on the .ii file.
Silent wrong result (assertions 2 and 3 FAILURE without any front-end
diagnostic) -- a soundness gap, not a conversion error.
2026-09-25: `__builtin_clzg' (the first failure) is supported now.
Remaining: "dropped the body of system-header function 'operator()'" at
<compare> line ~4076 (a comparison-category `__make' helper) and the
CONVERSION ERROR that follows.
